Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:00:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] docs: describe the porthole-dev fork and crossdirect's
 Rust handling

FORK.md says what this fork changes and why, how to install and pin it,
and how to rebase it onto upstream without regressing the APKBUILD
parser. AI.md and the notices at the top of README.md say how the fork is
made and that problems go here, not to postmarketOS.

docs/cross_compiling.md: crossdirect now compiles Rust that meson (or any
build system) passes to rustc directly for the right architecture, and
supports "cargo auditable build"; the caveat telling packagers to replace
it with "cargo build" is gone.

